  "narrative": "I interpret signed estimates as follows: for direction -1 claims, a positive estimate means stronger measured dependency in the exposed group, i.e. a more negative raw dependency_composite; for direction +1 claims, a positive estimate means a higher/less-negative raw composite, i.e. weaker measured dependency. H43 is the key new overall result: SMARCA4 loss is associated with a very large and precise stronger-dependency effect (+0.804, CI +0.742 to +0.867), so the previously validated marker-negative-stratum SMARCA4 association is not confined to that stratum; I accept it as a broad supplied-dataset association. H46 and H47 show that TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss remain very strong weaker/higher-composite associations when SMARCA4-loss cells are excluded (+0.816 and +0.803, respectively). Thus these accepted marker effects are not explained by SMARCA4 co-occurrence. H49 similarly shows that PTEN loss remains a moderate stronger-dependency association in a fully clean, SMARCA4-intact stratum (+0.260, CI +0.182 to +0.338), supporting independence of PTEN from the large TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4 axes. H45 shows PTEN loss is associated with stronger dependency within PIK3CA-mutant cells (+0.394, CI +0.156 to +0.631), although the exposed cell n=38 is small, so I accept this cautiously as a conditional dataset-level association. H50, H51, and H52 show that SMARCA4 loss remains strongly associated with stronger dependency within TP53-loss, KEAP1-loss, and PTEN-loss backgrounds (+0.815, +0.864, and +0.828), though the exposed cell sizes are smaller in those contexts, so the conclusion is supported but should be treated as context-specific and dataset-level rather than mechanism-confirmed. H54 does not support threshold-level CDKN2A loss in the stricter clean, SMARCA4-intact stratum: the point estimate is +0.148, just below the 0.15 threshold, and the interval crosses threshold; I keep it unresolved but defer further priority. H55 rejects BRCA2 loss as a stronger-dependency predictor in the clean stratum; the signed estimate is negative, i.e. opposite the pre-registered direction. H56 rejects ERBB2 amplification as a meaningful stronger-dependency predictor in the same stratum. H57 gives no clear support for research_signature_a >= 1 enhancing the SMARCA4-loss effect; the interaction is essentially null (+0.014), but the CI still reaches slightly above threshold, so I keep it unresolved/deferred rather than claiming absence of interaction. I request independent validation for H13, the KEAP1-loss main effect, because it is an accepted post-hoc reversal with very large precise discovery evidence but no independent validation; validating this protects against a post-hoc reversal or co-occurrence artifact. All claims remain associations in the supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Updated after iteration 4 appraise. Signed convention: direction -1 positive = stronger measured dependency; direction +1 positive = higher/less-negative composite = weaker measured dependency. Current strongest supplied-dataset associations: MSI_high -> stronger dependency (-1), robust in TP53-intact, TP53/KEAP1-intact, and Avana; pending clean+SMARCA4-intact test H48. TP53_loss -> weaker/higher composite (+1), robust in MSI-negative, KEAP1-intact, Avana, and SMARCA4-intact clean stratum H46. KEAP1_loss -> weaker/higher composite (+1) as formal reversal H13; robust in TP53-intact, TP53/MSI-clean, Avana, and SMARCA4-intact clean stratum H47; independent validation now requested for H13. PTEN_loss -> stronger dependency (-1), main accepted and independently validated; robust in TP53-intact, KEAP1-intact (validated), Avana, clean all-marker/SMARCA4-intact H49, and accepted cautiously in PIK3CA-mutant cells H45 (n=38 exposed, wide interval). SMARCA4_loss -> stronger dependency (-1), now accepted broadly overall H43 (+0.804, CI +0.742 to +0.867), previously accepted and independently validated in TP53/KEAP1/MSI-negative cells H40; SMARCA4 effect persists within TP53-loss clean H50, KEAP1-loss clean H51, and PTEN-loss clean H52, with smaller exposed cells but threshold-crossing intervals. Pending unresolved: CDKN2A reversal remains borderline and unresolved: H42 estimate +0.168 CI lower +0.100, stricter SMARCA4-intact H54 estimate +0.148 CI lower +0.093, not threshold-level enough to accept and no current validation request planned. H57 SMARCA4-by-research_signature_a interaction unresolved/deferred: near-null estimate +0.014 but CI upper +0.180, so interaction not established. H29/H30 TP53/MSI interactions remain deferred unresolved due small MSI-positive overlap cells. Pending untested or deferred: H48 MSI_high in clean+SMARCA4-intact; H53 SMARCA4 within MSI-positive cells; H44 SMARCA4-by-lineage interaction; H16-H18 lineage-specific accepted-marker checks; H23 PTEN in PIK3CA-wildtype. Negative/closed findings: lineage subtype main, KRAS, BRAF V600E, MTAP loss, STK11 overall, MYC amplification, EGFR amplification in pre-registered stronger-dependency direction, research markers d/e/f, STK11 in KEAP1-intact, RB1 in clean stratum, ARID1A in clean stratum, TP53-loss batch_a interaction, KEAP1-by-TP53 interaction, PTEN-by-PIK3CA original interaction, BRCA2 loss in clean SMARCA4-intact, ERBB2 amplification in clean SMARCA4-intact. Validation status before this request: H8, H28, H40 independently validated; H13 validation requested. Remaining new voluntary validation budget after this request: 7. Future priority if validation supports H13: confirm KEAP1 main as independently supported; consider later validation for broad SMARCA4 H43 if independent confirmation remains useful. All conclusions are dataset-level associations and do not establish causality or external generalizability.",
