  "narrative": "I interpret signed estimates consistently: for direction -1 claims, a positive estimate means stronger measured dependency in the exposed group; for direction +1 claims, a positive estimate means a higher/less-negative composite score, i.e. weaker measured dependency. The new independent validation for H13 is decisive: KEAP1 loss is associated with a higher/less-negative dependency score by +0.840 units, with an independent interval from +0.754 to +0.926 at the validation alpha, and the discovery estimate was +0.810 with CI +0.745 to +0.876. This is far above the 0.15 composite-unit threshold, so I accept KEAP1 loss as a strong supported supplied-dataset association with weaker measured dependency and close the main H13 investigation. The same validation reinforces rejection of the pre-registered H7 direction that KEAP1 loss would imply stronger dependency, because that signed estimate is negative, so H7 remains rejected and closed. KEAP1 loss remains robust in TP53-intact, MSI-negative, Avana, and clean SMARCA4-intact strata, and the KEAP1-by-TP53 interaction was rejected, so the main effect is not explained by TP53 co-occurrence. The current accepted supplied-dataset pattern is that TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss are large weaker-dependency associations, while MSI-high and SMARCA4 loss are large stronger-dependency associations and PTEN loss is a moderate validated stronger-dependency association. The newly closed validated claims are H7 original KEAP1 direction, H8 PTEN main, H28 PTEN in KEAP1-intact cells, H13 KEAP1 main, and H40 conditional SMARCA4 loss. Negative or unsupported findings include lineage-subtype main, KRAS, BRAF, MTAP, STK11 overall, MYC, EGFR original stronger-dependency direction, research markers D/E/F, STK11 in KEAP1-intact cells, RB1 and ARID1A in clean strata, BRCA2 loss and ERBB2 amplification in clean SMARCA4-intact cells, TP53-loss batch interaction, KEAP1-by-TP53 interaction, and PTEN-by-PIK3CA original interaction. Unresolved uncertainty remains for CDKN2A borderline reversal, TP53/MSI interactions with small MSI-positive cells, SMARCA4 within MSI-high cells where exposed cells are expected too small, lineage-specific accepted-marker checks, and the research-signature-A interaction. The most informative next analysis is H48, MSI-high tested in TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact cells if cell counts remain adequate; I defer H53 and H42 to avoid over-prioritizing small or borderline cells. I register APC-mutation and NF1-loss tests in the same clean SMARCA4-intact stratum as cautious residual discovery. At the next appraise, independent validation priority should consider H43 broad SMARCA4 main or one older large accepted marker. All conclusions are associations in the supplied dataset and do not establish causality or generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Updated after iteration 4 synthesis. Signed convention: direction -1 positive = stronger measured dependency; direction +1 positive = higher/less-negative composite = weaker measured dependency. Newly validated: H13 KEAP1 loss -> weaker/higher composite, discovery +0.810 CI +0.745 to +0.876, independent validation +0.840 interval +0.754 to +0.926; accepted and closed. H7 original KEAP1 stronger-dependency direction rejected/closed; validation signed -0.840. Other independently validated accepted claims: H8 PTEN loss stronger +0.239 discovery, validation +0.294; H28 PTEN in KEAP1-intact stronger +0.250 discovery, validation +0.240; H40 SMARCA4 loss in TP53/KEAP1/MSI-negative cells stronger +0.807 discovery, validation +0.793. Other strong accepted associations: TP53 loss -> weaker/higher +0.829 main, robust in MSI-negative +0.823, KEAP1-intact +0.800, Avana +0.830, clean SMARCA4-intact +0.816; MSI_high -> stronger +0.775 main, robust TP53-intact +0.761, TP53/KEAP1-intact +0.766, Avana +0.784, H48 pending clean SMARCA4-intact; KEAP1 loss -> weaker/higher +0.810 main validated, robust TP53-intact +0.780, TP53/MSI-intact +0.805, Avana +0.801, clean SMARCA4-intact +0.803; SMARCA4_loss -> stronger broad +0.804 main, conditional +0.793 validated, contexts TP53-loss clean +0.815, KEAP1-loss clean +0.864, PTEN-loss clean +0.828; PTEN_loss stronger moderate, main validated, KEAP1-intact validated, clean all-marker/SMARCA4-intact +0.260, PIK3CA-mutated +0.394 but n=38 exposed. Negative/closed: lineage subtype main, KRAS, BRAF, MTAP, STK11 overall, MYC, EGFR original stronger-dependency, research markers d/e/f, STK11 KEAP1-intact, RB1 clean, ARID1A clean, BRCA2 clean, ERBB2 clean, TP53 batch_a interaction, KEAP1 by TP53 interaction, PTEN by PIK3CA original interaction. Unresolved/deferred: CDKN2A borderline H42 +0.168 lower +0.100 and H54 +0.148 lower +0.093; H29/H30 TP53/MSI interactions small cells; H53 deferred due likely small SMARCA4-loss exposure within MSI_high; H16-H18 lineage marker checks deferred; H23 PTEN PIK3CA-wt deferred; H44 SMARCA4-by-lineage deferred; H57 research_signature_a interaction near-null. Active pending: H48 MSI_high in clean SMARCA4-intact if cells valid. New registered residual exploration: APC_mutation and NF1_loss in TP53/KEAP1/MSI/SMARCA4-intact cells with direction -1 and uncertain anticipated direction. Next appraise validation priority: H43 broad SMARCA4 main if independent confirmation remains useful; alternatives are H10 MSI_high or H11 TP53_loss because they are accepted but not independently validated; H8/H28/H40/H13 already validated. Keep all claims as dataset-level associations, not causal or generalizable."
